#import "../../collection.typ": paper-abstract, paper-keywords

#paper-abstract(language: "en")[
  Graph automorphisms of a Chevalley group correspond to each type of reduced
  indecomposable root system $Phi$, whose Coxeter graph has a non-trivial
  symmetry. It is well-known that a Chevalley algebra and its niltriangular
  subalgebra $N$ have a graph automorphism $theta$ exactly when $Phi$ is of type
  $A_n$ ($n >= 2$), $D_n$ ($n >= 4$) or $E_6$. We note connections with
  homomorphisms of root systems introduced in 1982.

  The main theorem on the centralizers in $N$ of the automorphism $theta$ gives
  new representations of niltriangular subalgebras, using also the unique series
  of unreduced indecomposable root systems of type $B C_n$.
]

#paper-keywords(language: "en")[
  Chevalley algebra, niltriangular subalgebra, homomorphisms of root systems.
]


